From u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com  Mon Dec 28 15:56:14 2020
From: u96353e7106735838 at groups.google.com (Karl Broman)
Date: Mon, 28 Dec 2020 15:56:14 +0000
Subject: Re: [Rqtl-disc] calculate multiple qtl with covariate and interacting covariate
Message-ID: <tamwB7YGLBI.GWLc8dOPBQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <tamwB7YGLBI.s4aAz4KPBQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
References: <tamwB7YGLBI.To_p_hCKBQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com> <tamwB7YGLBI.s4aAz4KPBQAJ@rqtl-disc.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/rqtl-disc/c/tamwB7YGLBI/m/GWLc8dOPBQAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The LOD scores from addcovarint() are for tests of the QTL x covariate interaction. In scanone, you'd take the difference between the LOD score with RL_C as interactive covariate and the LOD score when it is just an additive covariate. That the LOD score for the QTL x covariate interaction is small suggests that there is no evidence for the QTL effect being modified by RL_C value.

karl

